/target
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock IS tracked: this workspace builds deployed wasm binaries (an app),
# so pinning deps keeps CI reproducible — an unpinned wasm-bindgen drifted to a
# newer glue form than local and broke the Firefox patch in CI.
bin/
# wasm-pack output: ignore the generated .wasm/.js/package.json, but TRACK the
# .d.ts — it is the public TypeScript boundary surface. Committed + gated in CI
# (deploy.yml) so a #[wasm_bindgen] change cannot reshape the TS API silently.
# See docs/interface-audit-2026-07.md Part 1 #1. NB: ignoring `pkg/` (the dir)
# made the old `!*.d.ts` negation dead — git can't re-include a file whose parent
# dir is ignored — so we ignore the CONTENTS (`pkg/*`) instead.
crates/*/pkg/*
!crates/*/pkg/*.d.ts
wasm-pack.log
app/node_modules/
app/dist/
app/.tests-dist/
docs/*
.DS_Store
.claude
engineering-codex
CLAUDE.md